cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Noise Modelling Hanoi: smartphone-based urban noise measurement, modelling and agent-based simulation"
message: "If you use this software or these data, please cite them as below."
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Colauz/noise-modelling-hanoi"
abstract: >-
  A three-month study of what a low-cost smartphone protocol can and cannot
  establish about urban noise in Hanoi, Vietnam. 363 field measurements across
  three urban typologies, morphology features from OpenStreetMap, an evaluation
  framework using three cross-validation protocols, and an agent-based exposure
  simulation in GAMA. The delivered model is a three-parameter physical
  attenuation kernel, which outperforms every learned model tested under the
  reference protocol.
keywords:
  - urban noise
  - environmental acoustics
  - Hanoi
  - Vietnam
  - agent-based modelling
  - OpenStreetMap
  - reproducible research
  - negative results
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-11"

